,{"topic":"returns","text":"In FY2026 the company paid $22.3 billion to repurchase its own shares and $26.4 billion in dividends: $48.7 billion together (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["MSFT.buybacks.2026","MSFT.dividends.2026"]},{"topic":"quarter","text":"In the three months ended 2026-09-30 revenue was $92.3 billion, up 18.8% from $77.7 billion in the three months ended 2025-09-30.","cites":["MSFT.d.revenue.2026-07-01.2026-09-30","MSFT.d.revenue.2025-07-01.2025-09-30"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Over the four quarters to 2026-09-30 revenue added up to $346 billion (computed from five filed figures), operating income to $163 billion and net income to $143 billion.","cites":["MSFT.d.revenue.2025-10-01.2025-12-31","MSFT.d.revenue.2026-01-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.revenue.2025-07-01.2026-06-30","MSFT.d.revenue.2025-07-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.revenue.2026-07-01.2026-09-30","MSFT.d.opinc.2025-10-01.2025-12-31","MSFT.d.opinc.2026-01-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.opinc.2025-07-01.2026-06-30","MSFT.d.opinc.2025-07-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.opinc.2026-07-01.2026-09-30","MSFT.d.netinc.2025-10-01.2025-12-31","MSFT.d.netinc.2026-01-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.netinc.2025-07-01.2026-06-30","MSFT.d.netinc.2025-07-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.netinc.2026-07-01.2026-09-30"]},{"topic":"ttm","text":"Free cash flow over the same four quarters was $60 billion: operating cash flow of $196 billion less capital spending of $136 billion (computed from ten filed figures).","cites":["MSFT.d.ocf.2025-10-01.2025-12-31","MSFT.d.ocf.2026-01-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.ocf.2025-07-01.2026-06-30","MSFT.d.ocf.2025-07-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.ocf.2026-07-01.2026-09-30","MSFT.d.capex.2025-10-01.2025-12-31","MSFT.d.capex.2026-01-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.capex.2025-07-01.2026-06-30","MSFT.d.capex.2025-07-01.2026-03-31","MSFT.d.capex.2026-07-01.2026-09-30"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Remaining performance obligations - revenue under contract that was not yet recognised - were $684 billion at the end of FY2026, against $375 billion a year earlier. That is 206.1% of FY2026 revenue (computed from two filed figures).","cites":["MSFT.rpo.2026","MSFT.rpo.2025","MSFT.revenue.2026"]},{"topic":"backlog","text":"Deferred revenue was $75.7 billion at the end of FY2026 (tagged ContractWithCustomerLiability), against $67.3 billion a year earlier.","cites":["MSFT.deferred.2026","MSFT.deferred.2025"]},{"topic":"people","text":"The latest annual report gives the workforce as 223,000 in its own words. FY2026 revenue works out to about $1.5 million for each (computed from one filed figure and the number in that sentence).","cites":["MSFT.q.employees","MSFT.revenue.2026"]},{"topic":"debt","text":"At the end of FY2026 the balance sheet carried $20.9 billion in cash and cash equivalents and $55.9 billion in short-term investments, and $40.3 billion of debt as tagged (LongTermDebtNoncurrent + LongTermDebtCurrent). Cash and short-term investments exceeded that debt by $36.5 billion (computed from four filed figures).","cites":["MSFT.cash.2026","MSFT.sti.2026","MSFT.debtLong.2026","MSFT.debtCurrent.2026"]}]},"fin":{"MSFT":{}},"quotes":{"MSFT.q.employees":{"c":"MSFT","kind":"employees","n":223000,"quote":"As of June 30, 2026, we employed approximately 223,000 people on a full-time basis, 121,000 in the U.S. and 102,000 internationally.","source":"MSFT-0001193125-26-323660","section":"Item 1. Business","date":"2026-07-29","proof":"667ae89b16235db7891d1fe438eb31d6b2c507f757797f19fdd9c27da6deaefc"}}}